  "description": "Meet the Freego Maxx M3, a compact class 2 fat-tire electric bike designed for younger riders, students and adults who want powerful performance in an easy-to-handle package.\n\nPowered by a 600W rated, 750W peak motor, the M3 delivers responsive acceleration for campus commutes, neighborhood rides and everyday urban travel. Its 48V 13Ah battery provides an estimated range of 25–50 miles, depending on rider weight, terrain, riding mode and speed.\n\nThe compact frame, low 28.7-inch seat height and 16 × 4.0-inch fat tires offer confident handling and improved stability. Weighing approximately 55 lbs, the M3 is lighter and easier to lift, transport or fit into a vehicle than many full-size retro e-bikes.\n\nFor greater comfort and control, it comes equipped with front suspension, hydraulic disc brakes and a full-twist throttle. Multiple configurable riding modes support different regional and riding requirements. The throttle is limited to 20 mph, while pedal assist (PAS) provides assistance up to 28 mph.\n\nKey Features:\n\n600W rated / 750W peak motor\n\n48V 13Ah removable battery\n\nEstimated 25–50-mile riding range\n\nCompact 16 × 4.0-inch fat tires\n\nLow 28.7-inch seat height\n\nFront suspension for improved ride comfort\n\nHydraulic disc brakes\n\nFull-twist throttle\n\nApproximately 55 lb\n\n220-lb maximum payload\n\nRecommended rider height: 4'7\"–5'11\" (140–180 cm)\n\nIdeal for campus commuting and short urban trips",
